{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Heat shrink tubing fits my battery holder, relay and circuit board projects because it helps insulate the wired connections I make.",
    "Alligator clip leads fit the testing stage of those same projects, letting me try temporary connections before making them permanent."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The feeler gauge and coolant hose pliers solve specific problems I haven't shown a need for; being workshop tools doesn't make them useful to my circuit projects.",
    "The large hemostats seem awkward for small components, while glue accelerator, snap hooks and moisture absorbers address needs I haven't identified.",
    "The second heat shrink kit fits my interests, but choosing one kit already covers that need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been taken as broad interest in tools and hardware, although I choose supplies for particular tasks.",
    "A possible hobby use seems to count too much when the item's size or specialized purpose doesn't fit what I'm doing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my breadboards, battery holder, relay and PCB supplies matters: accessories for wiring and testing them are useful next steps.",
    "General usefulness isn't enough for me to choose something now. A caliper could help eventually, but I would wait for a project that requires precise measurements.",
    "My history spans years and includes separate practical needs, so a past hardware purchase doesn't necessarily indicate a current project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my electronics work but stretched that interest too broadly into tools and supplies without a clear current use."
}"}
